        <item>
            <title>0.76</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 07:53:34 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1791013537</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.76</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Addy now checks access when it launches. You sign in with GitHub, and if access is paused or a required update is pending, a gate window or sheet covers the workspace until it is resolved. While access is denied, workspace menu items and agent commands are disabled. A &quot;Check Again&quot; button re-runs the check, and the gate offers Sign Out, Update Now and Quit Addy.</li>
<li>Agent pane footers have a new &quot;Owned Panes&quot; button. It lists the panes that agent spawned with their status (Working, Idle, Done, Reported or Failed), and clicking a row reveals that pane, even if it is hidden or collapsed.</li>
<li>Addy Mobile can now</li>
<li>Start new chat or terminal agents in a project</li>
<li>Create branch worktrees</li>
<li>Switch an agent&#x27;s model and thinking level</li>
<li>Set an agent&#x27;s color</li>
<li>Remove, edit or reorder messages queued behind a running turn</li>
<li>Addy Mobile now mirrors your Mac&#x27;s model list, default models, sidebar project icons, and branch worktrees nested under each project, including branches of collapsed projects.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>The chat composer now has its own undo history. Inserting attachments, completing mentions and similar edits can be undone with Cmd+Z, and programmatic resets, such as after sending, no longer cause undo errors.</li>
<li>A pane&#x27;s &quot;working&quot; indicator now clears as soon as a turn finishes, instead of lingering until a two-minute timer expires.</li>
<li>Worktrees whose HEAD is detached, such as during a rebase or bisect, are now kept in the sidebar with their panes, chats and servers. Previously they were treated as removed. During a rebase the worktree keeps its branch name.</li>
<li>Selecting a project that is already showing now only restores its sidebar highlight. It no longer re-runs the project switch, which could steal keyboard focus on every sync.</li>
<li>The model list for the Antigravity CLI (agy) is preserved when a rescan fails, for example while the CLI updates itself. It no longer collapses to a single bundled entry.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Fixed chat agents appearing finished while the CLI was still running queued turns, such as a message sent mid-turn or a background-task notification. Chats now stay in the generating state until the last queued turn completes.</li>
<li>Fixed iCloud sync problems</li>
<li>Overlapping sends could re-send records that were already in flight.</li>
<li>A duplicate record in a batch could stall all pending saves.</li>
<li>A server copy identical to the local one kept re-triggering conflicts.</li>
<li>Partial send failures wrongly failed the whole Sync Now.</li>
<li>Sync Now&#x27;s local inventory became very slow with thousands of records, because it rewrote its journal for every record.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Internal Changes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Added a focus-change trace to help diagnose keyboard focus issues.</li>
<li>Remote protocol bumped to version 8.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
